BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1dec6d6bb433ea79384221664423aa3497d826b7@windsong-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261029T172710Z
SUMMARY:Newborn Basics Class @ THE BRIDGE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260512T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260512T113000
LOCATION:THE BRIDGE
CATEGORIES:Lifestyle Events
DESCRIPTION:Expecting a baby or adjusting to life with a newborn? Cook Chil
 dren’s is offering free Newborn Basics classes led by board‑certified 
 pediatricians to help parents feel confident and prepared.\nThese informat
 ive sessions cover:\nPreparing for the delivery\nBasic newborn care\nFeedi
 ng techniques\nSafe sleep tips\nCircumcision care\nUmbilical cord care\nVa
 ccination information\nGeneral safety information\nClasses will be held fr
 om 10:30 to 11:30 AM at THE BRIDGE on Tuesday\, May 12 with Dr. Alapati an
 d Tuesday\, May 19 with Dr. Kopalli—a great opportunity to ask questions
  and gain expert guidance as you begin your parenting journey.\nRegistrati
 on is required through Civic Rec.\nRSVP (5/12) : https://secure.rec1.com/T
 X/windsong-ranch-hoa-tx/catalog?filter=c2VhcmNoPTQyNzY5MzY=
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b32b41e042ac679f85a0d31d5b6c9c9f06da1b9e@windsong-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261029T172710Z
SUMMARY:Free Birds @ THE BRIDGE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260528T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260528T210000
LOCATION:THE BRIDGE
CATEGORIES:Lifestyle Events
DESCRIPTION:Calling All Free Birds!\nSave the date for the “Gnarly” Fre
 e Birds 80’s Party on Thursday\, May 28\, from 6 to 9 PM at THE BRIDGE! 
 Break out your leg warmers and denim jackets for a totally tubular night o
 f fun.\nCome dressed in your favorite 80’s outfit\, test your knowledge 
 during 80’s Music Bingo (with prizes for winners)\, and show off your sk
 ills with a Rubik’s Cube challenge. This event will be a potluck\, and a
  sign‑up sheet will be sent out in advance so we don’t all bring the s
 ame dish.\nInterested in joining Free Birds?\nFree Birds is a social club 
 for couples and singles in WSR who are empty nesters\, or almost empty nes
 ters\, looking to connect with like‑minded neighbors. The group typicall
 y meets monthly for themed events that include food\, drinks\, games\, and
  social time\, both onsite in WSR and at offsite locations.\nFor more info
 rmation\, contact WSR.freebirds@gmail.com or visit the group on Facebook a
 t Windsong Free Birds .
END:VEVENT
